      "message": "This looks like it should work, but I wonder if it might make more sense to introduce a new `raw_binary` build rule type rather than just a flag on `cc_binary`, as the way we are currently using `cc_binary` for this feels like a bit of a hack (relying on dead code removal to avoid including all the parts of libc and everything else which won\u0027t work in a bare-metal binary), and it\u0027s necessary to also set a bunch of other flags (`static_executable`, `nocrt`, `stl` and so on). If we added a new build rule it could do the right thing by default.\n\nThoughts?",
